{"version":"1","id":"bholmes","handle":"bholmes","name":"Ben Holmes","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--T_e2P4Sg--/f_auto/v1704628081/logos/bholmes.jpg","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-5.5327,"y":-7.2543,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":99,"newest_post_at":"2026-01-06T17:44:36.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2023-03-16T14:17:46.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.050505,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.10101,"avg_read_time":4.510204,"summary_length_avg":238.282609,"title_length_avg":55.444444,"title_length_var":491.438833,"tag_entropy":3.077257,"tag_diversity":0.555556,"top_tag_share":0.232323,"avg_upvotes":1.606061,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.111111,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.075,"zero_engagement_share":0.59596,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.950302,"non_article_ratio":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.03125},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-1.4853,6.5147],"cadence_depth":[-0.1765,-3.5294],"hype_variety":[8.2794,-1.1765],"title_style":[8.8088,-8.2059]},"top_tags":[["webdev",40],["react",39],["javascript",34],["css",17],["typescript",16],["tailwind-css",11],["nextjs",7],["frontend",6]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Astro fixed React server actions.","Stop using \"npm run.\" #javascript #webdevelopment #nodejs","\ud83d\udc40 Better Tailwind class management #tailwindcss #css #tutorial #javascript #webdevelopment"],"outlier":["\u269b\ufe0f React Context finally makes sense #programming #javascript #webdevelopment #tutorial #beginners"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"86fGnYBPp","title":"Using AI coding agents to build features end to end","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ciLXC1d2IVg","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-i-code-with-ai-in-2026-86fgnybpp","summary":"A developer shares their workflow for using AI coding agents (specifically Claude Opus 4.5) to build features end-to-end. The tutorial demonstrates adding an organization view to an iOS notes app, covering planning mode, voice transcription for requirements, custom rules configuration, phased implementation, context window management, code review processes, and PR creation. Key practices include breaking work into phases, using mockups for communication, setting concise response rules, staging commits strategically, letting agents complete changes before reviewing, and using fresh conversations when context degrades.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/ciLXC1d2IVg/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-01-06T17:44:36.000Z"},{"id":"ZITwzwlV1","title":"Swift's error handling advantages over JavaScript","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S2nWA8J-wts","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/swift-is-what-javascript-should-ve-been-for-errors--zitwzwlv1","summary":"Swift's error handling model offers significant advantages over JavaScript's approach. Swift functions explicitly declare whether they throw using the 'throws' keyword, require 'try' prefix when calling, and support pattern matching with enum-based error types. The language also provides a convenient 'try?' operator that converts errors to nil values, eliminating the need for split APIs between throwing and non-throwing functions. While Swift doesn't type-check specific error types (Rust does), its approach is more structured and developer-friendly than JavaScript's undocumented exception handling.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/S2nWA8J-wts/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-12-19T15:40:43.000Z"},{"id":"wZQx8jrlY","title":"I fixed Zustand's BIGGEST problem","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gXz-lLIJbMI","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/i-fixed-zustand-s-biggest-problem-wzqx8jrly","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/gXz-lLIJbMI/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-11-03T16:50:07.000Z"},{"id":"JLHxQaIam","title":"Making React desktop apps feel native with scroll behavior and tooltips","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9yPOXPFvQQs","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/building-desktop-apps-with-react-try-this-electron-or-tauri--jlhxqaiam","summary":"Learn how to make desktop apps built with React and Electron/Tauri feel more native by implementing proper scroll behavior using CSS overscroll-behavior properties and adding native tooltips with simple HTML title attributes. The guide covers handling nested scroll views, preventing unwanted page bouncing, and creating smooth user interactions that mirror native desktop applications.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/9yPOXPFvQQs/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-09-22T21:04:09.000Z"},{"id":"XboyR7It6","title":"Svelte simplifies async operations compared to React","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pvc6Y99nCuk","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/svelte-solved-react-s-biggest-problem-again-webdevelopment-tutorial-frontend-javascript-xboyr7it6","summary":"Svelte introduces a simplified approach to handling async operations that works on both server and client side without additional libraries. Unlike React, which requires server components or libraries like Tanstack Query for async data fetching, Svelte allows developers to use await directly with derived state to automatically rerun async operations when dependencies change. The framework also provides boundary concepts for handling loading and error states with custom UI components.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/pvc6Y99nCuk/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":5,"created_at":"2025-06-10T14:17:45.000Z"},{"id":"Yz06yDiw6","title":"Exploring the advantages of Go routines over JavaScript async","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WL4A0dqZBJE","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-makes-go-better-than-js-webdevelopment-backend-tutorial-yz06ydiw6","summary":"The post discusses the advantages of Go routines over JavaScript's async functions, highlighting Go's ability to efficiently handle concurrency through its scheduling system and channels, which improves performance and avoids slowdowns in single-threaded operations.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/WL4A0dqZBJE/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-05-19T14:09:02.000Z"},{"id":"leLv64UCA","title":"understanding streaming and websockets in AI apps","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NhSgzejNNHI","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/working-with-llms-learn-this-ai-webdevelopment-tutorial-beginners-lelv64uca","summary":"Learn about streaming and websockets in building AI applications. Understand the client-server interaction, differences in handling requests with protocols like HTTP and websockets, and see example code in Golang for real-time responses.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/NhSgzejNNHI/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-05-12T21:49:22.000Z"},{"id":"p0ZqUmMmH","title":"Enhance Tailwind CSS with data attributes and aria-pressed","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W-Wne_DCcN8","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/tailwind-devs-should-ditch-clsx-tutorial-webdevelopment-css-p0zqummmh","summary":"Using data attributes in Tailwind CSS can replace clsx for toggling classes in React, reducing the complexity of ternary operations. This approach not only simplifies the code but also promotes better accessibility by integrating ARIA attributes like aria-pressed. While it may result in longer class names, it aligns with Tailwind CSS conventions.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/W-Wne_DCcN8/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-04-08T13:43:26.000Z"},{"id":"lTPKqMFHe","title":"Run SQL in the browser using SQLite and web assembly","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MiaB247fOLg","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/you-can-put-sql-in-the-browser-now-tutorial-database-webdevelopment-ltpkqmfhe","summary":"It's now possible to run SQL directly in the browser using SQLite's web assembly build and the Origin Private File System, which allows browsers to read and write files. The SQLocal library can simplify querying and integrates with ORMs like drizzle. Chrome's dev tools facilitate debugging and querying using SQLite CLI.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/MiaB247fOLg/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-04-01T14:00:25.000Z"},{"id":"XRsCiM2aO","title":"Convert and compress files easily using terminal commands","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S6X_by_KJqY","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/stop-converting-images-with-sketchy-websites-tutorial-programming-commandline-xrscim2ao","summary":"Developers can use terminal commands to convert and compress images and videos instead of relying on untrusted websites. On Macs, the built-in zps can handle image conversion, while FFMPEG is a powerful tool for video conversion and audio extraction. Tools like warp terminal can assist in command usage and workflow automation.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/S6X_by_KJqY/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-03-17T15:22:18.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["lundeveloper","brancheducation","bitlemon","pezzzaswork","codebullet"],"opposite_handles":["horde","dailydevworld","watercooler","on_leuwcq","devtools"],"similar":[{"id":"lundeveloper","handle":"lundeveloper","name":"Lun Dev Code","is_squad":false,"x":-5.4206,"y":-7.2664,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":96,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--La2YlA9Z--/f_auto/v1723788819/logos/lundeveloper","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":1.317812,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.005208,"avg_read_time":6.59375,"tag_diversity":0.25},"top_tags_preview":[["css",42],["javascript",37],["html",26]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[7.75,5.1618],"cadence_depth":[-0.4559,1.5441],"hype_variety":[-1.2353,-7.6324],"title_style":[-7.7059,6.8529]}},{"id":"brancheducation","handle":"brancheducation","nam